.nh
.TH "PB-SSH-TRUST-HOST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-ssh-trust-host - Approve a changed SSH host identity


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb ssh trust-host <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Approve a pending SSH host-key change for a machine. Paperboat does not accept a changed
host identity on its own: check the pending SHA256 fingerprint out of band (for example on the
machine itself) before you trust it.

.PP
With --fingerprint the command trusts only if it equals the pending fingerprint; any other
value changes nothing. Without it, the command shows the current and pending fingerprints and
asks [y/N] in a terminal, and refuses outside one. --json needs --fingerprint. It does not run
OpenSSH.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--fingerprint\fP=""
	exact pending SHA256 fingerprint to trust (required outside a terminal and with --json)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for trust-host

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb ssh trust-host homelab
  pb ssh trust-host homelab --fingerprint SHA256:abc123
  pb ssh trust-host homelab --fingerprint SHA256:abc123 --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-ssh(1)\fP
